                },\n                {\n                    \"@type\": \"Question\",\n                    \"name\": \"What documents are required to sell a used generator in the UAE?\",\n                    \"acceptedAnswer\": {\n                        \"@type\": \"Answer\",\n                        \"text\": \"Sellers must provide commercial proof of ownership (original purchase invoice or commercial bill of sale), company trade license copy, authorized signatory Emirates ID, and a standard tax invoice including 5% UAE VAT.\"\n                    }\n                }\n            ]\n        }\n    ]\n}'),(852,1,'Selling Surplus Gensets After Building Handover: Tax & Invoice Guidelines','selling-surplus-generators-after-project-uae','Comprehensive technical breakdown of Selling Surplus Gensets After Building Handover: Tax & Invoice Guidelines for UAE engineering and procurement teams. Covers operational sizing, field protocol','<h2>Used Generator Valuation, Trading & Buyback: Selling Surplus Gensets After Building Handover: Tax &amp; Invoice Guidelines</h2>\n<div class=\"p-5 my-6 rounded-2xl bg-amber-50 border-l-4 border-amber-500 text-slate-800 text-sm leading-relaxed shadow-sm\">\n    <span class=\"text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-amber-800\">AEO Key Takeaway / Executive Summary</span>\n    <p class=\"mt-2 text-slate-700\">\n        <strong>Direct Answer for sell construction generator uae:</strong> In the United Arab Emirates, deploying and managing temporary power and modular site facilities requires compliance with ISO 8528-1:2018 performance classes, DEWA / ADDC electrical wiring regulations, and UAE Fire and Life Safety Code (FLSC 2018). Equipment operating in peak summer ambient temperatures of 50&deg;C requires continuous thermal derating (1.5% per 5&deg;C above 40&deg;C), certified 110% bunded environmental fuel containment, and scheduled 250-hour preventive maintenance to eliminate unplanned project downtime.\n    </p>\n</div>\n<p>The secon